.TH "pocket_calib" "1" "" "" "Pocket SDR"
.SH NAME
pocket_calib \- Antenna array attitude and per\-CH bias calibration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
pocket_calib [\-ts time] [\-te time] [\-f freq] [\-v]
             \-g geom_file \-n nav_file \-o out_file
             obs1 obs2 [obs3 ...]
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Estimate antenna\-array hardware delays (per\-element bias relative to CH1) and array attitude (roll / pitch / yaw) by per\-epoch EKF using per\-element RINEX OBS files and a RINEX NAV file.
The receiver position is first estimated from CH1 obs by single\-point positioning.
The array geometry is read from a body\-frame text file.
Calibration results are written to a text file consumable by \f[CR]pocket_trk\f[R] / \f[CR]pocket_sdr.py\f[R] for live beam\-forming.
.SH OPTIONS ([]: DEFAULT)
.TP
\f[CR]\-ts time\f[R], \f[CR]\-te time\f[R]
Start / end time (GPST, \f[CR]YYYY/MM/DD HH:MM:SS\f[R]) to use from the OBS files.
[all epochs]
.TP
\f[CR]\-f freq\f[R]
Frequency index used for calibration (0 = L1, 1 = L2, \&...).
[\f[CR]0\f[R]]
.TP
\f[CR]\-g geom_file\f[R]
Array geometry file.
One \f[CR]x y z\f[R] (m) per line in body frame (X = right, Y = forward, Z = up).
The k\-th line is the position of CH(k); the first line is CH1 (reference, must be \f[CR]0 0 0\f[R]).
.TP
\f[CR]\-n nav_file\f[R]
RINEX navigation data file.
.TP
\f[CR]\-o out_file\f[R]
Output text file.
Stores the estimated \f[CR]roll/pitch/yaw\f[R] and per\-CH bias.
.TP
\f[CR]\-v\f[R]
Print version and exit.
.TP
\f[CR]obs1 obs2 [obs3 ...]\f[R]
Per\-element RINEX OBS files.
The k\-th file is the obs file for CH(k).
At least 2 elements are required (typical: 4 or 8).
